  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 944 PM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nDry conditions continue through the remainder of the work week. A\nweak front on Wednesday will drop temperatures back to near\naverage, with a second backdoor cold front on Friday that will\ndrop temperatures to slightly below average, especially for the \nNE Panhandles. Where the main extent of the stronger area of LL \nCAA actually ends up is yet to be determined this many days out, \nbut favors areas east of the Mississippi at this time. By the \nweekend, a mid level disturbance as of the latest 08/00Z model and\nnumerical data shows could traverse the Panhandles and give some \nareas a low chance of some showers. High temperatures by the \nweekend will be near average for mid November.",
